Hello, our name is Customertimes , but you can call us CT. We are a global digital engineering, product development, and technology consulting company. Headquartered in New York, we have a team of 1000+ experts working across 65+ countries.
About this job:
Join a global enterprise transformation where you'll define the architecture behind business-critical Salesforce solutions used across multiple business functions. You'll own architectural decisions, establish engineering standards, and help shape the future Salesforce landscape while working alongside architects, engineers, and business leaders.
This is an opportunity to influence strategy—not just implementation.
Location: Europe (LATAM candidates may also be considered if able to work within CET hours)

What you'll do :

• Own end-to-end application architecture across Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, Experience Cloud, and Salesforce Data Cloud;

• Define scalable data models, security, governance, and application architecture standards;

• Design enterprise integrations between Salesforce, SAP, and external platforms;

• Lead the adoption of Salesforce Data Cloud, including identity resolution, unified customer profiles, segmentation, and activation;

• Create architecture roadmaps, solution designs, and technical documentation;

• Lead architecture reviews, technical workshops, and proof-of-concept initiatives;

• Mentor engineering teams and promote development best practices across Apex, LWC, Flows, and declarative solutions;

• Evaluate new Salesforce capabilities and drive continuous platform evolution.

What you'll bring :

• Experience as a Salesforce Application Architect, Solution Architect, or Technical Architect;

• Experience with Salesforce Consumer Goods Cloud or Retail Cloud, or commercial experience in the consumer goods or retail industry;

• Strong expertise across Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, and Experience Cloud;

• Hands-on architecture experience with Salesforce Data Cloud;

• Strong knowledge of Apex, LWC, Flows, APIs, security, and enterprise architecture principles;

• Experience designing integrations with SAP and other enterprise platforms;

• Ability to communicate architectural decisions to both technical and business stakeholders;

• Professional English.

You are a star if you have:

• Salesforce Application Architect or System Architect certification;

• Consumer Goods Cloud (CGC) experience;

• MuleSoft or other enterprise integration platforms;

• Experience in large-scale global transformation programs.

Why join us:

• Own architecture decisions for a strategic enterprise Salesforce platform;

• Lead the adoption of Salesforce Data Cloud and modern customer data capabilities;

• Design enterprise integrations connecting Salesforce, SAP, and other critical business systems;

• Influence engineering standards and mentor experienced development teams;

• Work with global stakeholders on a transformation program that delivers measurable business impact;

• Join a collaborative environment where architecture, innovation, and continuous improvement are valued.

What we offer you as a CTzen:
We call ourselves CTzens — a combination of the company's name and the word "citizen." This concept reflects who we are as coworkers and as people. Join our team and enjoy the perks that come with it:

•
Be rewarded for your impact with a competitive salary ;

•
Enjoy the freedom to work remotely — 100% remote opportunity ;

• Referral program;

• Flexible work schedule;

•
Learn, explore, and expand your expertise with access to the Udemy learning platform and free language courses, clear career tracks and personal development plan ;

•
Be a part of a supportive, global team ;

•
Take time to recharge with 20 working days of paid vacation leave and 5 days off on demand, and 15 working days of paid sick leave with a doctor's note ;

• Support for participation in professional development opportunities (webinars, conferences, training , etc.);

•
Stay connected through online team events, celebrations, and charity initiatives ;

•
Get recognized for your impact — earn CT points and exchange them for awesome merch .

If you're looking to contribute to global projects, grow your skills, shape the way you work, and be part of a connected international community — Customertimes is the place to build your next career chapter. Are you ready to spark the tech with us?

